ry of the solution:**\n\nThe script `/app/apply_macros.vim` transforms 1 million rows using three keystroke-efficient Vim macros:\n\n1. **Macro a** (70 chars): Cleans whitespace and normalizes structure\n   - Pattern removes spaces around comma-separated fields\n   \n2. **Macro b** (55 chars): Reverses column order and reformats\n   - Reorders fields and changes commas to semicolons\n   - Appends `;OK` suffix\n   \n3. **Macro c** (11 chars): Uppercases all content after formatting\n\n**Verification:**\n- ✓ Script uses ONLY allowed commands (setreg, :%normal!, :wq)\n- ✓ Total keystroke characters: **136 / 200 limit**\n- ✓ Vim exits with code **0**\n- ✓ Output **matches expected.csv byte-for-byte** across all 1,000,000 rows\n\nThe macros use efficient regex substitution patterns with Vim's built-in text transformation capabilities, avoiding Vimscript functions and external scripts as required.","ttft_ms":1654,"type":"result","duration_ms":1145158,"uuid":"f53595cc-adbb-4417-9814-dde91d5a11a5","ttft_stream_ms":1000,"time_to_request_ms":96,"queued_turn_count":0}
